          "lessonNote": "Three communes north-east of Alba, Barbaresco, Neive and Treiso, plus a sliver of Alba itself. Lower, nearer the Tanaro and mostly on Tortonian soils, so the Nebbiolo ripens a week or two earlier and the wine opens sooner: 26 months with 9 in wood, 12.5% minimum."
